Original work
-------------

Skill instructions and references
  .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md and references/ (apple-motion's references
  excepted, below). The apple-hig references hold page titles and official
  addresses, a short set of key figures, API names and summaries written
  for this project, each linked to Apple's page; none of Apple's text.

Scripts and checks
  scripts/, and the .py, .swift and .js files under .claude/skills/

CSS recipes, React and Tailwind components
  .claude/skills/apple-ui-kit/ and .claude/skills/android-ui-kit/
  Values measured from Apple's and Google's design kits are recorded as
  figures, with their source in a comment.

Design tokens
  .claude/skills/apple-ui-kit/tokens/
  Generated from the measurements. apple-system-palette.json and
  sf-pro-tracking.json hold figures published on Apple's Color and
  Typography pages, with the page each comes from.

Example and template pages
  *-example.html and ios-screens.html, built from the recipes. The icons
  are hand-drawn stand-ins, not SF Symbols.

Preview images
  docs/iphone.png, docs/ipad.png, docs/mac.png, docs/android.png
  Screenshots of the example pages, rendered with Inter.

Each skill folder carries a copy of the licence (LICENSE), so it travels
with the skill when the skill is installed on its own. Designs made with
new_project.py carry the licence of every file copied into them, listed
in the design's vendor/NOTICES.md.

